  "title": "# claude-md-chain: CLAUDE.md chain view in MD Studio + clean-up Brett, Nov 5 2026 (voice): \"Yeah, p…",
  "asked": "# claude-md-chain: CLAUDE.md chain view in MD Studio + clean-up Brett, Nov 5 2026 (voice): \"Yeah, put it in the MD studio. I want to be able to click root and then be able to see the Claude MD as the root and everything it's chained to. And when I select the things that it's chained to, I don't want it to read the files. I want it to list the rules with a switch. Actual file or what it says. It's the different notes that it says, the rules, the different things that it says, not the file itself. Every time it's going to update, I get a notification for approval. That's not a veto. It needs an approval.\" ## Build (MD Studio plugin) - A \"Claude chain\" view: a Root button shows the root CLAUDE.md and a tree of everything it pulls in (imports, @-references, linked rules files, _claude/rules, shared rules on axHub, instructions, memory files that sessions load, global ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md on the VPS). Show size per node and total loaded size; flag duplicates and dead links. - Selecting a node shows a LIST of the rules / instructions it states (one item per rule, short plain text, with heading + line ref), not the raw file. A switch per node: Rules | File. File = the raw markdown. - Duplicate / conflicting rules across files highlighted. - Any edit to a file in the chain (from MD Studio, CLI, API or a build) goes through a held axHub approval with policy confirm (NOT veto, no countdown, nothing runs without Brett's Approve). Approval shows file, diff summary, who asked. Add the rule to RULES.md too: builds must not edit chain files directly. - API / MCP / CLI / voice parity per the console rules. ## Clean-up proposal (no edits without approval) Audit the current chain and write a proposal in the report: one short root CLAUDE.md pointing to the rules, one rules file per project + one shared, archive the 237 KB handoff/context/CLAUDE.md copy and other duplicates. Submit each change as an approval; don't apply any yourself. Done: tests, desktop + phone shots in UI Review (non-blocking), readme, report `_claude/builds/reports/claude-md-chain.md`, THREADS row, PR to main handed to the merge queue (don't merge). No sub-agents, Opus only, never print secrets. Short plain report at the end. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once. Model switches: a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. Fable upgrades need no approval right now (Brett, Nov 4 2026: \"If it needs Fable, set it to be Fable\"): a step that needs Fable (schemas, asset types, contracts, engines/kernel, cross-app protocols) is set to Fable and runs on Fable; the switch is recorded on the build. Never launch a step on a higher model than it is pinned to: raise the step first.",
